# Omega, Heartless Evolution: "up to one" target, so Bot1 may choose none of Bot2's nonland permanents (an Ornithopter) and the
# trigger still resolves and Bot1 gains X life (CR 115.1d, 601.2c). X counts nonbasic lands Bot1 controls only (CR 205.4a): one
# Tropical Island, played on turn 1, counts and the Forest played on turn 3 does not, and Bot2's own nonbasic Underground Sea
# does not count either. Bot1 gains 1 (21); the Ornithopter is left untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Tropical Island
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Omega, Heartless Evolution
Forest x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Underground Sea
Ornithopter
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Tropical Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Underground Sea.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Omega, Heartless Evolution.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target()
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 21
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Underground Sea.Tapped = false
